  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the rule exist, and the rule is enabled and has run once with status `ok`.\n\n**Data view:** `Kibana Sample Data Logs` (`kibana_sample_data_logs`, time field `timestamp`). The fields that matter here are `response` (status code, with a `response.keyword` subfield), `bytes`, `clientip`, `url`, `geo.dest`, and `agent`.\n\n**Dashboard: `EFF-1865e5c9 Web logs overview`** (ID `e33d658d-283e-49a7-96c8-daf7facf3071`), six panels:\n- Total requests (count)\n- Unique visitors (unique count of `clientip`)\n- Average response size (average of `bytes`)\n- Total bytes served (sum of `bytes`)\n- Requests over time (ES|QL line chart)\n- Responses by status code (ES|QL bar chart)\n\nTime range is the last 7 days.\n\n**Alert rule: `EFF-1865e5c9 5xx spike`** (ID `9b9eb084-0e54-4778-abb7-413c0fbb627f`):\n- Elasticsearch query rule on the logs data view, with KQL `response.keyword : 5*`\n- Runs every 1 minute\n- Fires when the count is greater than 10 over a 5-minute window\n\nChoices I made that you may want to change:\n- **Wildcard for 5xx:** I used `5*` on the keyword field, which matches every code starting with 5.\n- **No actions attached:** The rule will record alerts but won't notify anyone. Adding a connector would be the next step.\n- **Dashboard time range:** I picked last 7 days.\n\n**Not verified:** This API key can't run ad-hoc queries here (the console, ES|QL, and search endpoints are disabled), so I didn't check the sample data's date range or the actual status-code counts. The 7-day window and the 5xx threshold are unchecked against the data.\n\n**API quirks:** The reference example for dashboard metrics and xy charts didn't validate as written. I adjusted the payload until Kibana accepted it.",
